1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
01 / Marketing decision workspace
Connect shopper evidence to a commercial hypothesis and a controlled test.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
02 / Supervised repurchase model
November top-20% precision: 67.8% forest vs 63.4% RFM. Historical, not causal.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
03 / Actual fitted-model inference
Changing a coherent behavior profile recalculates the probability and model-path drivers.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:27,000
04 / Learned product factors
SVD hit-rate@5: 27.9% vs 14.4% popularity among eligible novel-product shoppers.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,000
05 / Read the contribution outcome
Synthetic example: conversion improves, but the contribution interval crosses zero.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:43,000
06 / Source-backed evidence retrieval
Fitted TF-IDF retrieval returns existing passages and sources; it is not a generative LLM.

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
07 / Commercial assumptions made explicit
Include discounts on baseline purchases, break-even conversion and test sample size.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
08 / Auditable evidence and limits
50 Python checks plus browser-engine reference tests. No invented campaign results.
